<body>
<div class="poster">

  <!-- HEADER -->
  <div class="header">
    <div class="header-badge">IPCC Sixth Assessment Report &middot; 2023</div>
    <h1>Climate Change 2023: <span>Key Findings</span></h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A synthesis of the most critical findings from the IPCC AR6 cycle — the most comprehensive scientific assessment of climate change to date. Human-caused climate change is already affecting every region on Earth.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- SEVEN HEADLINE METRICS -->
  <div class="metrics-section">
    <div class="section-label">&#9632; Seven Headline Metrics</div>
    <div class="metrics-grid">
      <div class="metric-card">
        <div class="metric-value">+1.1°C</div>
        <div class="metric-unit">Temperature</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Global surface warming<br>2011–2020 vs 1850–1900</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-card">
        <div class="metric-value">410</div>
        <div class="metric-unit">ppm CO₂</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Highest concentration<br>in 2 million years (2019)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-card">
        <div class="metric-value">~59</div>
        <div class="metric-unit">GtCO₂e</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Global greenhouse gas<br>emissions in 2019</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-card">
        <div class="metric-value">~500</div>
        <div class="metric-unit">GtCO₂</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Remaining carbon budget<br>for 1.5°C (50% chance)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-card highlight">
        <div class="metric-value">43%</div>
        <div class="metric-unit">Reduction</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Required GHG cut by 2030<br>for 1.5°C pathway</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-card">
        <div class="metric-value">0.20m</div>
        <div class="metric-unit">Sea Level</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Global mean rise<br>1901–2018</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-card highlight">
        <div class="metric-value">3.3–3.6B</div>
        <div class="metric-unit">People</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Highly vulnerable to<br>climate hazards</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- HIGHLIGHT BANNER -->
  <div class="pop-highlight">
    <div>
      <div class="pop-highlight-value">3.3–3.6 <span class="pop-highlight-unit">billion</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pop-highlight-text">
      people live in contexts <strong>highly vulnerable to climate change</strong>. Climate hazards increasingly interact with poverty, inequality, and ecosystem degradation to produce <strong>cascading and compounding risks</strong> affecting food security, water access, health, and biodiversity worldwide.
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- MAIN CONTENT GRID -->
  <div class="content-area" style="margin-top: 20px;">

    <!-- SECTION 1: OBSERVED CHANGES -->
    <div class="section observed">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-number">1</div>
        <div class="section-title">Observed Changes</div>
      </div>
      <div class="section-body">
        Every region has experienced increases in frequency and intensity of extreme weather events — heatwaves, heavy precipitation, droughts, and tropical cyclones — with clear attribution to human influence.
      </div>
      <div class="indicator-table">
        <div class="indicator-row">
          <div class="indicator-dot" style="background:#fbbf24"></div>
          <div class="indicator-name">Global surface temperature rise</div>
          <div class="indicator-val">+1.1°C</div>
        </div>
        <div class="indicator-row">
          <div class="indicator-dot" style="background:#fb923c"></div>
          <div class="indicator-name">Atmospheric CO₂ (2019)</div>
          <div class="indicator-val">410 ppm</div>
        </div>
        <div class="indicator-row">
          <div class="indicator-dot" style="background:#f97316"></div>
          <div class="indicator-name">Global GHG emissions (2019)</div>
          <div class="indicator-val">~59 GtCO₂e</div>
        </div>
        <div class="indicator-row">
          <div class="indicator-dot" style="background:#ea580c"></div>
          <div class="indicator-name">Sea level rise (1901–2018)</div>
          <div class="indicator-val">~0.20 m</div>
        </div>
        <div class="indicator-row">
          <div class="indicator-dot" style="background:#ef4444"></div>
          <div class="indicator-name">Arctic sea ice decline (Sep)</div>
          <div class="indicator-val">~40%</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 2: FUTURE PROJECTIONS -->
    <div class="section projections">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-number">2</div>
        <div class="section-title">Future Projections (SSP Scenarios)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="section-body">
        Temperature trajectories diverge sharply depending on emissions pathway. Under the highest scenario, warming could exceed 4.4°C by 2100.
      </div>
      <div class="ssp-chart">
        <div class="ssp-row">
          <div class="ssp-label">SSP1-1.9</div>
          <div class="ssp-bar-track">
            <div class="ssp-bar" style="width:31.8%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #14b8a6, #0d9488);">
              <span class="ssp-temp">1.4°C</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ssp-row">
          <div class="ssp-label">SSP1-2.6</div>
          <div class="ssp-bar-track">
            <div class="ssp-bar" style="width:40.9%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #3b82f6, #2563eb);">
              <span class="ssp-temp">1.8°C</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ssp-row">
          <div class="ssp-label">SSP2-4.5</div>
          <div class="ssp-bar-track">
            <div class="ssp-bar" style="width:61.4%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #f59e0b, #d97706);">
              <span class="ssp-temp">2.7°C</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ssp-row">
          <div class="ssp-label">SSP3-7.0</div>
          <div class="ssp-bar-track">
            <div class="ssp-bar" style="width:81.8%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #f97316, #ea580c);">
              <span class="ssp-temp">3.6°C</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ssp-row">
          <div class="ssp-label">SSP5-8.5</div>
          <div class="ssp-bar-track">
            <div class="ssp-bar" style="width:100%; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #ef4444, #991b1b);">
              <span class="ssp-temp">4.4°C</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ssp-desc">Sea level: 0.28–0.55 m (SSP1-1.9) to 0.63–1.01 m (SSP5-8.5) by 2100</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 3: RISKS & IMPACTS -->
    <div class="section risks">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-number">3</div>
        <div class="section-title">Risks & Cascading Impacts</div>
      </div>
      <div class="risk-grid">
        <div class="risk-item">
          <div class="risk-icon">🌾</div>
          <div class="risk-title">Food Security</div>
          <div class="risk-desc">Crop yield growth slowing; fisheries productivity declining in tropical zones</div>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-item">
          <div class="risk-icon">💧</div>
          <div class="risk-title">Water Stress</div>
          <div class="risk-desc">Over half the world faces severe water scarcity for ≥1 month per year</div>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-item">
          <div class="risk-icon">🏥</div>
          <div class="risk-title">Human Health</div>
          <div class="risk-desc">Heat-related mortality and vector-borne disease ranges expanding</div>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-item">
          <div class="risk-icon">🦎</div>
          <div class="risk-title">Biodiversity</div>
          <div class="risk-desc">Up to 14% terrestrial species at very high extinction risk at 1.5°C</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 4: MITIGATION PATHWAYS -->
    <div class="section mitigation">
      <div class="section-header">
        <div class="section-number">4</div>
        <div class="section-title">Mitigation & Adaptation Pathways</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pathway-compare">
        <div class="pathway-box target-15">
          <div class="pathway-target">1.5°C</div>
          <div class="pathway-label">Target Pathway</div>
          <div class="pathway-stat">
            <span class="pathway-stat-label">By 2030</span>
            <span class="pathway-stat-value" style="color:#14b8a6">−43%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pathway-stat">
            <span class="pathway-stat-label">Net Zero CO₂</span>
            <span class="pathway-stat-value">~2050</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pathway-stat">
            <span class="pathway-stat-label">Carbon Budget</span>
            <span class="pathway-stat-value">~500 Gt</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pathway-box target-2">
          <div class="pathway-target">2.0°C</div>
          <div class="pathway-label">Target Pathway</div>
          <div class="pathway-stat">
            <span class="pathway-stat-label">By 2030</span>
            <span class="pathway-stat-value" style="color:#3b82f6">−27%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pathway-stat">
            <span class="pathway-stat-label">Net Zero CO₂</span>
            <span class="pathway-stat-value">~2070</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pathway-stat">
            <span class="pathway-stat-label">Carbon Budget</span>
            <span class="pathway-stat-value">~1150 Gt</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="levers-list">
        <div class="lever-item"><div class="lever-dot"></div>Rapid decarbonization of energy systems</div>
        <div class="lever-item"><div class="lever-dot"></div>Electrification of transport</div>
        <div class="lever-item"><div class="lever-dot"></div>Demand-side efficiency improvements</div>
        <div class="lever-item"><div class="lever-dot"></div>Protection &amp; restoration of carbon sinks</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 5: NARROWING WINDOW -->
    <div class="narrowing-window">
      <div class="narrowing-header">
        <div class="narrowing-number">5</div>
        <div class="narrowing-title">The Narrowing Window for Action</div>
      </div>
      <div class="narrowing-content">
        <div class="narrowing-text">
          The choices made <strong>in this decade</strong> will determine whether warming can be held to 1.5°C or 2°C. Delayed action increases costs, locks in high-carbon infrastructure, and reduces the feasibility of limiting warming. Climate finance flows remain <strong>insufficient — falling short by a factor of 3 to 6</strong> for adaptation alone. Immediate, deep, and sustained emissions reductions across all sectors are essential to secure a liveable and sustainable future for all.
        </div>
        <div class="narrowing-callout">
          <div class="narrowing-callout-label">Climate Finance Gap</div>
          <div class="narrowing-callout-value">3–6×</div>
          <div class="narrowing-callout-desc">Shortfall for adaptation needs</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- FOOTER -->
  <div class="footer">
    <div class="footer-source">Source: IPCC, 2023. AR6 Synthesis Report: Climate Change 2023. Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change.</div>
    <div class="footer-branding">Climate Science Conference 2023</div>
  </div>

</div>

